(Regression test: a missing map key sets _last_error, but a later
successful map key lookup clears it so a subsequent On error does not fire.)

A map called m is {"a": 1, "b": 2}.
A number called bad is m's "missing".
On error print "first".

A number called bad2 is m's "also missing".
A number called good is m's "a".
On error print "second".
